{% if collection.handle == 'electric-dirt-bikes' and all_products['t-01'] != blank and all_products['t-02'] != blank %}
  {{ 'pq-buying-guide.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <section class="pq pq-buying-guide" aria-labelledby="BuyingGuide-{{ section.id }}">
    <div class="pq-container">
      <h2 class="pq-buying-guide__heading" id="BuyingGuide-{{ section.id }}">Choose your Panquire electric dirt bike</h2>
      <p>Compare two electric dirt bikes for adult recreational off-road riding. Start with your riding experience, fit, battery needs and total budget, then explore the model that suits your plans.</p>
      {% render 'pq-dirt-bike-selection' %}
      <div class="pq-buying-guide__columns">
        <div><h3>60V or 72V?</h3><p>The <a href="{{ all_products['t-01'].url }}">60V Panquire T-01</a> is the lower-priced option. The <a href="{{ all_products['t-02'].url }}">72V Panquire T-02</a> has more nominal battery energy and a higher stated peak output. Voltage alone does not establish acceleration, range or handling; compare the complete bike and the conditions in which you plan to ride.</p></div>
        <div>
          {% if cart.currency.iso_code == 'USD' and all_products['t-01'].price < 300000 and all_products['t-02'].price < 300000 %}
            <h3>Electric dirt bikes under US$3,000</h3>
          {% else %}
            <h3>Set your complete riding budget</h3>
          {% endif %}
          <p>Compare the live bike prices above with your budget, including protective equipment, taxes, duties and upkeep. A bike price below a budget ceiling does not guarantee a delivered total below that ceiling. Prices and availability can change.</p>
          {% if cart.currency.iso_code == 'USD' and all_products['t-01'].price < 200000 %}<p>The T-01's current listed bike price is under US$2,000. Check the final checkout total before deciding whether it fits your complete budget.</p>{% endif %}
          <p>For alternatives to Sur-Ron and other brands, use our <a href="{{ pages.compare.url | default: '/pages/compare' }}">electric dirt bike comparison</a> to review model-specific tradeoffs.</p>
        </div>
        <div><h3>Check fit and riding access</h3><p>Both models list a recommended rider height of approximately 160–190 cm. Height guidance is only a starting point: confidence, inseam and suspension setup matter too. The suspension rider-weight guidance is separate from maximum load. Confirm that your intended riding location permits the exact vehicle.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Plan for ownership</h3><p>Both bikes use removable batteries, chain drive and three electronic power levels with no clutch. Ask about compatible replacement parts and maintenance before purchase. The one-year limited warranty covers the motor, battery and controller, subject to the <a href="{{ pages.tos.url | default: '/pages/tos' }}">current warranty terms</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pq-buying-guide__faq">
        <h2>Electric dirt bike buying questions</h2>
        <details><summary>Which Panquire model should I choose?</summary><p>Choose T-01 if the lower bike price is your priority. Consider T-02 if you want more nominal battery capacity and stated peak power. Compare fit and riding needs as well as specifications. Neither peak power nor price alone establishes suitability for a new rider.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How far can I ride on one charge?</summary><p>T-01 lists up to 80 km in Eco mode and T-02 up to 90 km in Eco mode. These are stated ranges, not a guarantee for fast or demanding trail riding. Terrain, temperature, speed and rider weight affect actual distance.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I remove the battery for charging?</summary><p>Both models have removable batteries. Use only the charger specified for the exact model: 6A for T-01 and 18A for T-02. Review the product page and owner's instructions for charging conditions and handling.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Are these road-legal electric bicycles?</summary><p>Do not assume that these electric dirt bikes qualify as Class 1, 2 or 3 bicycles. Vehicle classification, road and trail access, registration, licensing and insurance depend on the jurisdiction. Confirm the requirements for your exact bike and riding location before purchase.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What should I check before ordering?</summary><p>Review current stock, the final price, supported delivery destinations, estimated timing and warranty terms. For parts compatibility, fit or other questions, <a href="{{ pages.contact.url | default: '/pages/contact' }}">contact Panquire support</a> with your intended model and destination.</p></details>
      </div>
      <div class="pq-buying-guide__links"><a href="{{ all_products['t-01'].url }}">Explore the T-01</a><a href="{{ all_products['t-02'].url }}">Explore the T-02</a><a href="{{ pages.compare.url | default: '/pages/compare' }}">Compare with other brands</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
{% endif %}
{% schema %}
{"name":"Dirt bike buying guide","enabled_on":{"templates":["collection"]},"settings":[],"presets":[{"name":"Dirt bike buying guide"}]}
{% endschema %}
